# 1 Three numbers this volume actually derived

@widths 3264 6528
| Quantity | This volume | Measurement / full theory |
| a_e | α/(2π)=0.00116141 | 0.00115965218073(28) (CODATA) |
| Lamb 2s–2p | leading log ~10³ MHz, Uehling −27 MHz | 1057.845(9) MHz |
| α⁻¹ | 137.036 at q²=0; electron log only at large q | α⁻¹(M_Z)≈127.95 (PDG) |

The one-loop anomaly accounts for all but about 0.15% of a_e. The omitted 0.15% is (α/π)² and higher, plus a hadronic vacuum-polarization piece below 10⁻¹² and a still smaller weak piece. Lesson 15's “one part in a billion” is the comparison after those higher orders, not the comparison of α/(2π) with experiment. Quoting a billionth from this volume's one-loop formula would be a false advertisement.

### Worked example 1

Compute the relative error of the one-loop anomaly. (0.00116141−0.00115965)/0.00115965≈0.00152, one and a half parts per thousand of a, matching the expected size of the two-loop term, which is of order α/π times the one-loop term.

# 2 The Lamb interval as a qualitative test

Dirac hydrogen has no 2s–2p interval. Measuring 1057.8 MHz is therefore not a more precise value of a number the tree theory already had; it is the existence of an effect the tree theory forbids. Lessons 76–77 derived the two leading mechanisms and their signs. They did not produce 1057.845 from a complete numerical evaluation, and this lesson will not pretend they did.

# 3 Running, with an honest coefficient

Lesson 68's formula α(q²)=α/[1−(α/3π)log(|q²|/m²)] includes one charged fermion, the electron. From q=m_e to q=M_Z the electron logarithm is (α/3π)log(M_Z²/m_e²)≈0.006, a 0.6% shift of α, or about one unit in α⁻¹. The measured shift, 137.036→127.95, is ten units. The extra nine come from muons, taus, and quarks, each adding to Π with a coefficient 1/3 per charged lepton and 3Q²/3 per quark colour. This course computed the mechanism and the electron term. It did not compute α(M_Z).

### Worked example 2

Why does a quark with charge 2/3 contribute 4/9 times as much as a lepton of charge 1, times N_c=3? Vacuum polarization is proportional to Q², and three colours multiply that by 3, so 3×(4/9)=4/3 of a lepton. Up-type quarks therefore out-weight electrons in the running, which is why the electron-only logarithm underestimates the shift to M_Z.

# 4 What a discrepancy would mean

Lesson 67 absorbed an ultraviolet log into m₀. That logic does not become false if a_μ, after every Standard-Model diagram, disagreed with storage-ring data. Such a disagreement, if it survived, would be additional amplitudes: extra particles in the muon loop, extra operators, an incomplete hadronic evaluation. It would not license discarding mass renormalization, any more than a wrong tree-level Compton formula would license discarding Maxwell's equations. The muon anomaly is not settled in this volume and is not used as a premise.

