# Summary

1. One-loop a_e matches experiment to 0.15%; the rest is higher orders this volume does not compute.

2. The Lamb interval is a qualitative QED effect; 1058 MHz is measured, 1040 MHz and −27 MHz are the pieces derived here.

3. The electron running is a 0.6% effect to M_Z; the full shift is larger because other charged fermions contribute.

4. “One part in a billion” is not a claim about α/(2π) alone.

5. A residual discrepancy would be new amplitudes, not a license to abandon renormalization.

