# Solutions

**1.** 1/(2π×137.036)=0.00116141.

**2.** About 0.15% of a_e.

**3.** Two-loop and higher QED; hadronic vacuum polarization; a weak (Z,W) piece.

**4.** The Dirac theory predicts zero for 2s−2p; a nonzero measurement is the existence of loops, not a refined digit of a tree-level formula.

**5.** (α/3π)log((91×10⁹/5.11×10⁵)²)≈(1/1290)×log((1.78×10⁵)²)≈0.006, a 0.6% increase of α.

**6.** Muons, taus, and quarks also run the coupling.

**7.** Nothing: m=m₀+A(m₀²) would still hold. Extra amplitudes would be added on top.

**8.** 1057.845(9) MHz (Lundeen and Pipkin).

**9.** Lesson 75, Section 3.

**10.** 3[(2/3)²+(2/3)²+(−1/3)²]=3[4/9+4/9+1/9]=3= three times one electron, for u,c,t counted as two charge-2/3 and one charge-1/3 per generation. (A generation is one up-type, one down-type, times colour: 3[(2/3)²+(−1/3)²]=3(4/9+1/9)=5/3 of an electron.)

